---
import { list } from "~/lib/content";
import DefList from "~/components/ui/DefList.astro";
import Section from "~/components/ui/Section.astro";

const principles = await list("principles");
---

<Section id="learned" title="What I’ve learned">
  <DefList items={principles.map((data) => ({ term: data.title, detail: data.text }))} />
  <div class="story">
    <p class="story__h">From the IPv6 move</p>
    <p>
      After we moved the clusters to IPv6-only, apps started hanging when they connected to a database. The
      database had a dual-stack address, so the apps resolved both an IPv4 and an IPv6 address, and the IPv6
      connections hung because the security group only allowed IPv4. Allowing IPv6 there fixed it. The bigger
      lesson: IPv6-only egress only works with DNS64 and NAT64, so everything around the clusters needs
      testing too.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .story {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: var(--radius-s);
      max-width: 46em;
    }

    .story__h {
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }

    .story p:not(.story__h) {
      color: var(--ink-muted);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
  }
</style>
